# 必考词 Unit21
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit21核心词汇

{{urge}}{{/ɜːdʒ}}{{v./n. 催促； urge；冲动}}{{He urged the committee to reconsider the decision.}}
{{utilize}}{{/ˈjuːtəlaɪz}}{{v. 利用； utilize}}{{The company utilizes renewable energy sources.}}
{{utter}}{{/ˈʌtər}}{{v./adj. 说出； utter；完全的}}{{He didn't utter a single word during the meeting.}}
{{vacant}}{{/ˈveɪkənt}}{{adj. 空的； vacant；空缺的}}{{There are several vacant positions in the company.}}
{{vague}}{{/veɪɡ}}{{adj. 模糊的； vague；不明确的}}{{The instructions were too vague to follow.}}
{{valid}}{{/ˈvælɪd}}{{adj. 有效的； valid；合理的}}{{The ticket is valid for three months.}}
{{vanish}}{{/ˈvænɪʃ}}{{v. 消失； vanish}}{{The ship vanished without a trace.}}
{{variable}}{{/ˈveəriəbl}}{{adj./n. 可变的； variable；变量}}{{The experiment has many variables.}}
{{vary}}{{/ˈveəri}}{{v. 变化； vary；不同}}{{Prices vary depending on the quality.}}
{{vast}}{{/vɑːst}}{{adj. 巨大的； vast；广阔的}}{{The country has vast natural resources.}}
{{venture}}{{/ˈventʃər}}{{n./v. 冒险； venture；风险投资}}{{He started a new business venture.}}
{{verdict}}{{/ˈvɜːdɪkt}}{{n. 裁决； verdict；判断}}{{The jury reached a unanimous verdict.}}
{{verify}}{{/ˈverɪfaɪ}}{{v. 核实； verify；证实}}{{Please verify the information before publishing it.}}
{{versatile}}{{/ˈvɜːsətaɪl}}{{adj. 多才多艺的； versatile；多功能的}}{{She is a versatile actress who can play any role.}}
{{version}}{{/ˈvɜːʃn}}{{n. 版本； version；说法}}{{The new version of the software includes many improvements.}}
{{versus}}{{/ˈvɜːsəs}}{{prep. 对； versus；与…相对}}{{The match is Team A versus Team B.}}
{{veteran}}{{/ˈvetərən}}{{n./adj. 老兵； veteran；经验丰富的}}{{He is a veteran of the advertising industry.}}
{{via}}{{/ˈvaɪə}}{{prep. 通过； via；经由}}{{The message was sent via email.}}
{{violate}}{{/ˈvaɪəleɪt}}{{v. 违反； violate；侵犯}}{{The company violated environmental regulations.}}
{{violent}}{{/ˈvaɪələnt}}{{adj. 暴力的； violent；猛烈的}}{{The protest turned violent.}}
{{virtual}}{{/ˈvɜːtʃuəl}}{{adj. 虚拟的； virtual；实质上的}}{{The virtual conference attracted thousands of participants.}}
{{visible}}{{/ˈvɪzəbl}}{{adj. 可见的； visible；明显的}}{{The results of the policy are clearly visible.}}
{{vital}}{{/ˈvaɪtl}}{{adj. 至关重要的； vital；生命的}}{{Water is vital for human survival.}}
{{vivid}}{{/ˈvɪvɪd}}{{adj. 生动的； vivid；鲜明的}}{{She gave a vivid description of the accident.}}
{{volume}}{{/ˈvɒljuːm}}{{n. 体积； volume；音量；卷}}{{The volume of trade has increased this year.}}
{{voluntary}}{{/ˈvɒləntri}}{{adj. 自愿的； voluntary}}{{Participation in the program is voluntary.}}
{{vote}}{{/vəʊt}}{{v./n. 投票； vote；表决}}{{Everyone has the right to vote.}}
{{vow}}{{/vaʊ}}{{v./n. 发誓； vow；誓言}}{{She vowed never to make the same mistake again.}}
{{vulnerable}}{{/ˈvʌlnərəbl}}{{adj. 脆弱的； vulnerable；易受伤的}}{{Children are particularly vulnerable to the disease.}}
{{wage}}{{/weɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 工资； wage；进行（战争）}}{{The government raised the minimum wage.}}
{{wander}}{{/ˈwɒndər}}{{v. 漫步； wander；走神}}{{He wandered through the streets of the old town.}}
{{ward}}{{/wɔːd}}{{n. 病房； ward；行政区}}{{The patient was moved to a different ward.}}
{{warrant}}{{/ˈwɒrənt}}{{n./v. 授权令； warrant；保证}}{{The police obtained a search warrant.}}
{{weave}}{{/wiːv}}{{v. 编织； weave；编造}}{{The story weaves together several different narratives.}}
{{weigh}}{{/weɪ}}{{v. 权衡； weigh；称重}}{{You should weigh the pros and cons before deciding.}}
{{weird}}{{/wɪərd}}{{adj. 奇怪的； weird}}{{There was something weird about the situation.}}
{{welfare}}{{/ˈwelfeər}}{{n. 福利； welfare；幸福}}{{The government cut welfare spending.}}
{{whereas}}{{/weərˈæz}}{{conj. 然而； whereas；鉴于}}{{He is tall, whereas his brother is short.}}
{{whisper}}{{/ˈwɪspər}}{{v./n. 低语； whisper}}{{She whispered the secret in his ear.}}
{{wholesale}}{{/ˈhəʊlseɪl}}{{n./adj. 批发； wholesale；大规模的}}{{The goods are sold at wholesale prices.}}
{{wield}}{{/wiːld}}{{v. 行使； wield；挥舞}}{{The president wields enormous power.}}
{{withdraw}}{{/wɪðˈdrɔː}}{{v. 撤回； withdraw；取款}}{{He withdrew his application for the position.}}
{{withhold}}{{/wɪðˈhəʊld}}{{v. 扣留； withhold；隐瞒}}{{The company withheld information from the public.}}
{{witness}}{{/ˈwɪtnəs}}{{n./v. 目击者； witness；见证}}{{Several witnesses testified in court.}}
{{worship}}{{/ˈwɜːʃɪp}}{{v./n. 崇拜； worship；礼拜}}{{The temple is a place of worship.}}
{{wrap}}{{/ræp}}{{v./n. 包裹； wrap；围巾}}{{She wrapped the gift in colorful paper.}}
{{yield}}{{/jiːld}}{{v./n. 产出； yield；让步}}{{The farm yields a large crop of wheat.}}
{{zone}}{{/zəʊn}}{{n. 地区； zone；地带}}{{The area has been designated as a no-fly zone.}}
{{abstract}}{{/ˈæbstrækt}}{{adj./n. 抽象的； abstract；摘要}}{{The concept is too abstract for young children.}}
{{abundant}}{{/əˈbʌndənt}}{{adj. 丰富的； abundant}}{{The region has abundant natural resources.}}
{{academic}}{{/ˌækəˈdemɪk}}{{adj./n. 学术的； academic；学者}}{{She pursued an academic career in physics.}}
{{access}}{{/ˈækses}}{{n./v. 接入； access；访问}}{{Students have access to the library 24 hours a day.}}
{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳； accommodate； accommodating}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 300 guests.}}
{{account}}{{/əˈkaʊnt}}{{n./v. 账户； account；解释}}{{Can you account for the missing money?}}
{{accurate}}{{/ˈækjərət}}{{adj. 准确的； accurate}}{{The report provides an accurate picture of the situation.}}
{{accuse}}{{/əˈkjuːz}}{{v. 指控； accuse；谴责}}{{He was accused of stealing the money.}}
{{acknowledge}}{{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{v. 承认； acknowledge；致谢}}{{The company acknowledged the error and apologized.}}
{{acquisition}}{{/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn}}{{n. 获得； acquisition；收购}}{{The acquisition of the company cost $2 billion.}}
{{adapt}}{{/əˈdæpt}}{{v. 适应； adapt；改编}}{{It is important to adapt to new circumstances.}}
{{adequate}}{{/ˈædɪkwət}}{{adj. 足够的； adequate}}{{The funding is not adequate for the project.}}
{{adjust}}{{/əˈdʒʌst}}{{v. 调整； adjust；适应}}{{You need to adjust the settings on the machine.}}
{{administration}}{{/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn}}{{n. 管理； administration；政府}}{{The new administration introduced several reforms.}}
{{adopt}}{{/əˈdɒpt}}{{v. 采纳； adopt；收养}}{{The company adopted a new strategy for growth.}}
{{advance}}{{/ədˈvɑːns}}{{v./n. 进步； advance；预付}}{{Technology continues to advance at a rapid pace.}}
{{advocate}}{{/ˈædvəkeɪt}}{{v./n. 提倡； advocate；拥护者}}{{She advocates for equal rights for all citizens.}}
{{affect}}{{/əˈfekt}}{{v. 影响； affect；感动}}{{The drought affected crops across the region.}}
{{afford}}{{/əˈfɔːd}}{{v. 负担得起； afford；提供}}{{I can't afford to buy a new car right now.}}
{{agenda}}{{/əˈdʒendə}}{{n. 议程； agenda；目的}}{{The topic was added to the meeting agenda.}}
{{aggressive}}{{/əˈɡresɪv}}{{adj. 侵略性的； aggressive；有进取心的}}{{The company has an aggressive marketing strategy.}}
{{alert}}{{/əˈlɜːt}}{{adj./v./n. 警觉的； alert；警报}}{{The government issued a health alert.}}
{{allocate}}{{/ˈæləkeɪt}}{{v. 分配； allocate；拨出}}{{The funds were allocated to different departments.}}
{{alter}}{{/ˈɔːltər}}{{v. 改变； alter；修改}}{{The plan was altered to accommodate new requirements.}}
{{alternative}}{{/ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv}}{{adj./n. 替代的； alternative；选择}}{{We need to find an alternative solution.}}
{{ambitious}}{{/æmˈbɪʃəs}}{{adj. 有雄心的； ambitious}}{{She is an ambitious young professional.}}
{{amend}}{{/əˈmend}}{{v. 修正； amend；改善}}{{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}
{{ample}}{{/ˈæmpl}}{{adj. 充足的； ample}}{{There is ample evidence to support the theory.}}
{{analyze}}{{/ˈænəlaɪz}}{{v. 分析； analyze}}{{The data was analyzed by a team of experts.}}
{{annual}}{{/ˈænjuəl}}{{adj. 年度的； annual}}{{The company publishes an annual report.}}
{{anticipate}}{{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 预期； anticipate；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}
{{apparent}}{{/əˈpærənt}}{{adj. 明显的； apparent；表面上的}}{{It was apparent that the plan had failed.}}
{{appeal}}{{/əˈpiːl}}{{v./n. 呼吁； appeal；上诉}}{{The charity made an appeal for donations.}}
{{appetite}}{{/ˈæpɪtaɪt}}{{n. 食欲； appetite；欲望}}{{The scandal diminished public appetite for reform.}}
{{appliance}}{{/əˈplaɪəns}}{{n. 器具； appliance；家用电器}}{{The kitchen is equipped with modern appliances.}}
{{applicable}}{{/əˈplɪkəbl}}{{adj. 适用的； applicable}}{{The rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{appoint}}{{/əˈpɔɪnt}}{{v. 任命； appoint；指定}}{{She was appointed as the new director.}}
{{appreciate}}{{/əˈpriːʃieɪt}}{{v. 感激； appreciate；理解；升值}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{approach}}{{/əˈprəʊtʃ}}{{v./n. 接近； approach；方法}}{{We need a different approach to the problem.}}
{{appropriate}}{{/əˈprəʊpriət}}{{adj. 适当的； appropriate}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the event.}}
{{approve}}{{/əˈpruːv}}{{v. 批准； approve；赞成}}{{The committee approved the budget proposal.}}
